; xfail: unexpected operand
;
; Missing-separator mis-parse: `if x g()` (intent: `if x` then `g()`) parses as
; a greedy condition operand list `x g()`, with the newline as the if/consequent
; separator — so `return 0` below is stolen as the consequent and the intended
; `g()` is folded into the condition. `x` is a bare non-callable value, so the
; trailing operand `g` cannot attach; collapse_operand_sequence# used to silently
; drop it (the whole `if` degenerated to nothing). It now reports "unexpected
; operand - missing operator, or a ':'/newline separator before this statement".
; The fix is narrow — only a bare non-callable value (not a method chain, not a
; delegate) followed by a non-operator triggers it, so valid parenless calls
; (`recv.method arg`, `g arg` for a delegate) and infix operators (incl. name
; operators like `mod` and word operators `and`/`or`) are unaffected.
; Self-hosted-only.

function g() returns int
    3

function main() returns int
{
    let x true
    if x g()
    return 0
}
